Generative Agents Lab
=====================

This project reimplements the architecture described in:

  Joon Sung Park, Joseph C. O'Brien, Carrie J. Cai, Meredith Ringel Morris,
  Percy Liang, and Michael S. Bernstein. 2023. Generative Agents: Interactive
  Simulacra of Human Behavior. UIST '23. arXiv:2304.03442v2.

Third-party material derived from joonspk-research/generative_agents
(commit fe05a71d3e4ed7d10bf68aa4eda6dd995ec070f4), Copyright 2023 Joon Sung Park,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (copy in
third_party/generative_agents/LICENSE):

  * scenarios/smallville_n25/ and scenarios/pilot*/: persona fields, history
    statements and spatial-memory trees converted from
    environment/frontend_server/storage/base_the_ville_n25/ and
    base_the_ville_isabella_maria_klaus/, and agent_history_init_n25.csv /
    agent_history_init_n3.csv. Changes: converted to YAML/JSON, split into
    seed statements, and (under the default candidacy_seed_policy) one
    statement removed for Jennifer Moore, as documented in
    docs/reproduction_spec.md (A-5, D-3).
  * scenarios/smallville_n25/map/: the_ville tile matrices and special-block
    tables converted to a compact JSON form. Changes: format only.
  * prompts/: several templates adapt the wording and information scope of the
    released prompt templates (persona/prompt_template/v2, v3_ChatGPT) and the
    prompts printed in the paper. Changes: restructured, versioned, and given
    JSON output schemas.

Not included: the game art (tilesets, character sprites) credited in the
official README to PixyMoon, LimeZu and pipohi. Those assets carry their own
terms; the viewer here draws simple shapes instead.
